# hush config — copy to .env (gitignored), then bring up the stack:
#
#   cd cmd/hush
#   cp .env.example .env                  # then edit it (the REQUIRED block)
#   docker compose up --build             # → http://localhost:8080
#
# No DATABASE_URL or CLICKHOUSE_DSN here, and no localhost anywhere: the app
# reaches its database and observation store by the compose SERVICE names
# (postgres, clickhouse), and docker-compose.yml builds those connection
# strings from the credentials below and the service names. The database
# connection is configured once, in the compose file, not in here. The
# database is internal to the stack — only the web port is published — so
# these credentials never leave it.
#
# hush fails to start if anything in the REQUIRED block below is unset: the
# Beach stack (Postgres + ClickHouse), Cloudflare R2 + Images, and a real mail
# transport are not optional. A misconfigured hush exits with the missing list.

# The internal Postgres: the login the postgres service is created with, and
# what compose builds the app's DATABASE_URL from. Defaults are fine for an
# internal-only database; change them if you want, in this one place.
POSTGRES_USER=beach
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=beach
POSTGRES_DB=hush

# Absolute origin for links inside outgoing email. Defaults to
# http://localhost:8080; set it to your real public origin in production so
# verification and invite links point at the right place.
#BASE_URL=https://hush.example.com

# First-boot password for the seeded admin account. Required when RELEASE is
# set (production). Unset in dev, the password is "password".
#HUSH_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Cloudflare Turnstile — required when RELEASE is set. The managed widget
# sits on login, apply, register, and invite. Unset in dev = no widget.
#TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
#TURNSTILE_SECRET=

# ════════════════════════════ REQUIRED ════════════════════════════════════
# hush will not boot without all of this set.

# ── Mail transport (REQUIRED: configure Mailgun OR SMTP) ───────────────────
# Verification and invite mail must be able to leave the process. Set EITHER
# the Mailgun pair, OR the SMTP host (+ creds). See mailer/mailer.go.
MAIL_FROM_NAME=hush
MAIL_FROM_ADDR=hush@example.com
MAILGUN_KEY=
MAILGUN_DOMAIN=
#SMTP_HOST=
#SMTP_PORT=587
#SMTP_USERNAME=
#SMTP_PASSWORD=

# ── Cloudflare R2 (REQUIRED) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Durable file bytes: application photos + the Cloudflare-Images delivery-URL
# fallback. Set all four; R2_PUBLIC_URL is optional (unset = presigned links).
R2_ENDPOINT=accountid.r2.cloudflarestorage.com   # the bucket's S3 API host (no scheme)
R2_BUCKET=hush                                    # bucket name; one store per bucket
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=                                 # R2 API token key pair (dashboard -> R2 -> API tokens)
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://files.example.com          # public/custom-domain base for stable URLs; unset = presigned 1h links

# ── Cloudflare Images (REQUIRED) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Image posts upload here, served resized from imagedelivery.net. Set all three
# credentials; the variants are created in the CF dashboard ("public" full-size,
# "thumb" a ~600px square crop, fit: cover, for the grid tiles).
CF_IMAGES_ACCOUNT_ID=                             # account id (dashboard -> images -> overview)
CF_IMAGES_TOKEN=                                  # api token with Cloudflare Images edit permission
CF_IMAGES_HASH=                                   # delivery hash, the first path segment of imagedelivery.net urls
#CF_IMAGES_VARIANT=public                         # full-size variant feed cards render (default "public")
#CF_IMAGES_THUMB=public                           # wall-print source (default "public"; set to "thumb" if you create that variant)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The points a verified email is worth on the author track. Baked into the
# reputation engine at boot, so it stays env (unlike the policy seeds below).
#HUSH_EMAIL_POINTS=2

# ── First-boot policy seeds ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The gate-and-moderation policy lives in the DATABASE and is edited live at
# /admin/settings — no restart. These vars only SEED an empty hush_settings
# table on first boot; once seeded the database is authoritative and changing
# them here does nothing.
#HUSH_TIER1=3            # author score that unlocks tier 1 (the profile + invites)
#HUSH_TIER2=8            # author score that unlocks tier 2 (DMs)
#HUSH_FLAG_TIER=1        # a flag from this tier or above insta-hides a post
#HUSH_FLAG_QUORUM=3      # this many tier-0 flags hide a post by agreement
#HUSH_INVITE_BASE=3      # a tier-1 member's starting invite allowance
#HUSH_INVITE_MAX=6       # invite hard cap, however high the chain climbs
#HUSH_OPEN_SLOTS=0       # first-come registrations with no review; 0 = queue only
#HUSH_ADMIN_EMAIL=       # where new-application notices go; blank = none
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
